# cm_unattributed_commit.baseline — grandfathered unattributed commits (BOB-162)
#
# Consumed by: scripts/hooks/unattributed-commit-guard.sh --range HEAD --baseline <this file>
# (pre-build invariant 63, CM-UNATTRIBUTED-COMMIT-RATCHET).
#
# Operator decision (binding, recorded as DATA per §11.4.224(E) / §11.4.66):
# option (b) of BOB-162 — a ONE-TIME monotone-decrease ratchet. Every commit
# listed below was already in history when the gate was adopted; any other
# unattributed bare/templated commit reachable from HEAD FAILS the gate.
#
# Grandfathering is by EXACT commit SHA (never by count): a new commit is never
# in this set by construction, even if it reuses a grandfathered subject line.
# The guard also refuses the two ways to hide a new commit here:
#   * more rows than SEEDED_COUNT  -> FAIL (the set may only shrink);
#   * a row committed after SEED_CUTOFF_EPOCH -> FAIL (cannot grandfather it).
# A row inside the scanned range that is no longer a violation FAILs as
# RETIRED — delete it in the same change. History is never rewritten to shrink
# this set (§11.4.113); it shrinks only if the closed pattern set changes.
#
# Seeded 2026-09-27T15:12:05Z from HEAD 30221da: 26 commits reachable from HEAD (24 bare
# "Auto-commit" incl. 1 epoch-ms-suffixed, 2 "sync: ..."); a scan of --all
# refs finds the same 26. Cross-checked by an independent subject-line count
# of HEAD history (also 26) with a zero-hit negative control. The earlier
# "14 since the last tag" figure was a range artefact: the default range is
# now 1.3.0..HEAD and holds 0, which is exactly why the gate scans all of HEAD.
# (cutoff = committer time of the NEWEST grandfathered commit, not the seed time,
#  so nothing committed after the last grandfathered one can ever be added)
# SEED_CUTOFF_EPOCH: 1789833444
# SEEDED_COUNT: 26
